**What made G-1 honest**

The catalog asks whether a transient fetch failure is negatively cached with a short TTL and distinguished from a genuine 404. Live `platform/plugin/cache.py` only had content-addressed `put`/`get`, so that question could not pass.

`Cache.fetch` / `lookup_named` now record:

| outcome | type | ttl |
|---|---|---|
| 5xx / transport error | `negative-transient` | 5s |
| HTTP 404 | `negative-absence` | 60s |
| 2xx | `positive` | 3600s |

After the negative TTL, the next lookup hits the network again. Existing `put`/`get` are unchanged.

